  "blocks": [
   {
    "id": "t0",
    "kind": "h",
    "text": "Solidity &mdash; Solidity 0.8.39-develop documentation",
    "inView": true
   },
   {
    "id": "t1",
    "kind": "p",
    "text": "Solidity is an object-oriented, high-level language for implementing smart contracts.",
    "inView": true
   },
   {
    "id": "t2",
    "kind": "p",
    "text": "Smart contracts are programs that govern the behavior of accounts within the Ethereum state.",
    "inView": true
   },
   {
    "id": "t3",
    "kind": "p",
    "text": "Solidity is a curly-bracket language designed to target the Ethereum Virtual Machine (EVM).",
    "inView": true
   },
   {
    "id": "t4",
    "kind": "p",
    "text": "It is influenced by C++, Python, and JavaScript.",
    "inView": true
   },
   {
    "id": "t5",
    "kind": "p",
    "text": "You can find more details about which languages Solidity has been inspired by in the language influences section.",
    "inView": true
   },
   {
    "id": "t6",
    "kind": "p",
    "text": "Solidity is statically typed, supports inheritance, libraries, and complex user-defined types, among other features.",
    "inView": true
   },
   {
    "id": "t7",
    "kind": "p",
    "text": "With Solidity, you can create contracts for uses such as voting, crowdfunding, blind auctions, and multi-signature wallets.",
    "inView": true
   },
   {
    "id": "t8",
    "kind": "p",
    "text": "When deploying contracts, you should use the latest released version of Solidity.",
    "inView": true
   },
   {
    "id": "t9",
    "kind": "h",
    "text": "Apart from exceptional cases, only the latest version receives",
    "inView": true
   },
   {
    "id": "t10",
    "kind": "p",
    "text": "Furthermore, breaking changes, as well as new features, are introduced regularly.",
    "inView": true
   },
   {
    "id": "t11",
    "kind": "p",
    "text": "We currently use a 0.y.z version number to indicate this fast pace of change .",
    "inView": true
   },
   {
    "id": "t12",
    "kind": "p",
    "text": "The Solidity 0.8.x release introduced a lot of breaking changes.",
    "inView": true
   },
   {
    "id": "t13",
    "kind": "p",
    "text": "Make sure you read the full list .",
    "inView": true
   },
   {
    "id": "t14",
    "kind": "h",
    "text": "Ideas for improving Solidity or this documentation are always welcome,",
    "inView": false
   },
   {
    "id": "t15",
    "kind": "p",
    "text": "read our contributors guide for more details.",
    "inView": false
   },
   {
    "id": "t16",
    "kind": "h",
    "text": "You can download this documentation as PDF, HTML or Epub",
    "inView": false
   },
   {
    "id": "t17",
    "kind": "p",
    "text": "by clicking on the versions flyout menu in the bottom-right corner and selecting the preferred download format.",
    "inView": false
   },
   {
    "id": "t18",
    "kind": "h",
    "text": "1. Understand the Smart Contract Basics",
    "inView": false
   },
   {
    "id": "t19",
    "kind": "p",
    "text": "If you are new to the concept of smart contracts, we recommend you to get started by digging into the “Introduction to Smart Contracts” section, which covers the following:",
    "inView": false
   },
   {
    "id": "t20",
    "kind": "p",
    "text": "A simple example smart contract written in Solidity.",
    "inView": false
   },
   {
    "id": "t21",
    "kind": "p",
    "text": "The Ethereum Virtual Machine .",
    "inView": false
   },
   {
    "id": "t22",
    "kind": "p",
    "text": "Once you are accustomed to the basics, we recommend you read the “Solidity by Example”",
    "inView": false
   },
   {
    "id": "t23",
    "kind": "p",
    "text": "and “Language Description” sections to understand the core concepts of the language.",
    "inView": false
   },
   {
    "id": "t24",
    "kind": "h",
    "text": "3. Install the Solidity Compiler",
    "inView": false
   },
   {
    "id": "t25",
    "kind": "h",
    "text": "There are various ways to install the Solidity compiler,",
    "inView": false
   },
   {
    "id": "t26",
    "kind": "p",
    "text": "simply choose your preferred option and follow the steps outlined on the installation page .",
    "inView": false
   },
   {
    "id": "t27",
    "kind": "h",
    "text": "You can try out code examples directly in your browser with the",
    "inView": false
   },
   {
    "id": "t28",
    "kind": "p",
    "text": "Remix is a web browser-based IDE that allows you to write, deploy and administer Solidity smart contracts,",
    "inView": false
   },
   {
    "id": "t29",
    "kind": "p",
    "text": "without the need to install Solidity locally.",
    "inView": false
   },
   {
    "id": "t30",
    "kind": "p",
    "text": "As humans write software, it can have bugs.",
    "inView": false
   },
   {
    "id": "t31",
    "kind": "p",
    "text": "Therefore, you should follow established software development best practices when writing your smart contracts.",
    "inView": false
   },
   {
    "id": "t32",
    "kind": "p",
    "text": "This includes code review, testing, audits, and correctness proofs.",
    "inView": false
   },
   {
    "id": "t33",
    "kind": "h",
    "text": "Smart contract users are sometimes more confident with code than their authors,",
    "inView": false
   },
   {
    "id": "t34",
    "kind": "p",
    "text": "and blockchains and smart contracts have their own unique issues to watch out for,",
    "inView": false
   },
   {
    "id": "t35",
    "kind": "p",
    "text": "so before working on production code, make sure you read the Security Considerations section.",
    "inView": false
   },
   {
    "id": "t36",
    "kind": "p",
    "text": "If you want to learn more about building decentralized applications on Ethereum,",
    "inView": false
   },
   {
    "id": "t37",
    "kind": "p",
    "text": "the Ethereum Developer Resources can help you with further general documentation around Ethereum,",
    "inView": false
   },
   {
    "id": "t38",
    "kind": "p",
    "text": "and a wide selection of tutorials, tools, and development frameworks.",
    "inView": false
   },
   {
    "id": "t39",
    "kind": "h",
    "text": "If you have any questions, you can try searching for answers or asking on the",
    "inView": false
   }
  ],
